  "note": "Three hand-authored personas for the Genetics Assessment grader. gradeGenetics(state) builds a context (Manchester score from the per-band counts, Bethesda criteria met, external PREMM5 percent or null, external Tyrer-Cuzick lifetime or 0, affected first-degree relatives = parents/siblings/children with affectedWithCancer 'yes' AND a non-empty cancers list, early-onset count using age <= 50 inclusive across relatives AND proband, paediatric < 18, tumour-spectrum booleans), runs 23 rules in catalogue order and returns riskLevel = max severity of the fired rules ('low' when nothing fires), plus manchesterScore/bethesdaMet/premm5Score/tyrerCuzickLifetime and firedRules. Flags are SPLIT: form-app.js calls detectAdditionalFlags(state) with the state only (it re-runs gradeGenetics internally), mirrored by flagsArgs [\"state\"]; flags are stable-sorted high > medium > low. Quirks verified: the Manchester rules are mutually exclusive bands (15-19 / 20-29 / >= 30) while GEN-BET-001 and GEN-BET-002 are cumulative; GEN-FAM-002 uses === 2 so 3+ affected FDRs fire only GEN-FAM-001; hasMaleBreast tests type.includes('male breast'), and 'female breast'.includes('male breast') is TRUE, so any relative cancer typed 'Female breast ...' spuriously fires GEN-TUM-001 (BUG, pinned by the moderate persona); a proband's own male breast cancer is never detected (proband loop only checks ovarian/pancreatic/bilateral); FLAG-COUN-001 fires on priorGeneticCounselling '' as well as 'no'; FLAG-LINE-001/002 need the OTHER side to list <= 1 aunts/uncles + cousins in total, affected or not; the Tyrer-Cuzick >= 17 boundary is inclusive. The 'timestamp' key is added by form-app.js, not the grader. Regenerate expected with: bin/test-personas genetics-assessment --update",
